esp32s3: a Wi-Fi radio, from the C3's models

The S3 had no Wi-Fi radio: Wi-Fi start-up hung in the PHY's calibration
(ram_read_sar2_code polling 0x6000E050, where nothing was mapped), so the
library's S3 Wi-Fi sketches never got past WiFi.begin or a scan. The S3's
radio blocks are the C3's generation at the C3's addresses, so lcgamboa's
C3 models serve:

- When a session asks for the radio (-nic ...,model=esp32c3_wifi), the S3
  machine maps the C3's analog I2C master (0x6000E000), PHYA, FE and power
  manager models, FE2 and the baseband (NRX, BB) as the C3 machine does,
  and the C3's Wi-Fi MAC at 0x60033000 on the S3's interrupt matrix, with
  its MAC address from the S3's eFuses. Without that NIC nothing changes.
- The S3's SENS (patch 0004) reports the internal temperature sensor
  ready, reading about 25 degC: the PHY reads it at start-up.

So that the C3's MAC model can share the xtensa program with the ESP32's:
the two models defined the same global functions (Esp32_sendFrame,
Esp32_WLAN_frame_delivered) and QOM type name (esp32_wifi). Each now sets
its frame functions in the shared Esp32WifiState, which the shared access
point code calls through; the C3 model's type is esp32c3_wifi (the C3
machine creates it by that name); and esp32_wifi_channel is defined once,
in esp32_wifi_ap.c, rather than in both analog models.

Written for esp32bench (GPL-2.0-or-later). Changes lcgamboa's and
Espressif's hw/misc/esp32_wifi.c, esp32c3_wifi.c, esp32_ana.c,
esp32c3_ana.c, esp32_wifi_ap.c, their headers, hw/riscv/esp32c3_picsimlab.c,
hw/xtensa/esp32s3.c and hw/misc/meson.build (GPL-2.0-or-later; notices
kept). Applied by esp32bench (core/crates/sim/src/lcgamboa.rs) to
lcgamboa/qemu at 885a6e7061fb70fac78a074a719423810bc19a17, after patch 0011.

